2186549593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549902 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549902 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549902 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549902 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549902 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549902 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186549751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549902 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d506de6d-4e6d-5568-a53f-79ffc50374e1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549928 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186549902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549928 #edb/ref 1069 "q-35908" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549928 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549928 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the range of the function $y=f(x)=(x-1)^{2}-3?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549928 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0bc8d353-4f35-531e-9326-d4dcbc01bbdb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549928 #edb/ref 1074 "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=1$ and $k=-3,$ the vertex is $(1,-3).$\n\n- Since $a=1>0,$ the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output. \n\nTherefore, the range is $[-3,\\infty ).$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/26/265532f4f4726151444ed873b875fc62c3c32a690a0ac859a318e2d4dc8fd285.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549998 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186549862 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549998 #edb/ref 1069 "q-90975" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549998 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549998 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the range of the function $f(x)={x}^{2}+1?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549998 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c749b226-6df0-583d-9d39-da82636ab3b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549998 #edb/ref 1074 "The given parabola is written in standard form,\n\n$$\ny=a{x}^{2}+bx+c,\n$$\n\nwith $a=1>0,$ $b=0,$ and $c=1.$\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}=-\\frac{0}{2\\cdot 1}=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=0$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}+1 \\\\  & =(0)^{2}+1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(0,1),$ and the range of the function is $[1,\\infty ).$\n\n![](images/0a/0a0bb7cbd5494106b36e85f4b9f2604153d28623883c33f507e1ef36389999c4.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560357 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186561069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560357 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186561071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560357 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186561083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560357 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560357 #edb/ref 1045 "Domain and Range of Quadratic Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560357 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186561069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560357 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560357 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560357 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "cd1774d0-cc54-52b2-8fb3-b23040b59b85" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560403 #edb/ref 1080 "[-4,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560403 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560403 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "12e9b9ea-0207-5775-8719-53fb983a237d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560478 #edb/ref 1080 "[2,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560478 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218656047