592186560542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560874 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560874 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560874 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186560542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560874 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "20d40415-4aca-5a00-a88c-3b8ead6018b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560931 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560931 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560931 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560931 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560931 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560752 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560931 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560931 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560931 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186560580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560931 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9e3ba704-088a-57fb-bc54-70440ac77e83" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560961 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186560640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560961 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560961 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560961 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186560640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186560961 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e8c25361-0058-5188-b424-05769d00535f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561015 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561015 #edb/ref 1069 "q-90983" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561015 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561015 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the range of the function $f(x)=-5(x-1)(x-2)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561015 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "723435c8-f6c2-5011-8005-6ac70ede7884" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561015 #edb/ref 1074 "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny=a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}),\n$$\n\nwith $a=-5<0.$ \n\nBecause the leading coefficient is negative, the parabola opens downward. Consequently, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=2,$ and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{1+2}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=\\frac{3}{2}$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5(x-1)(x-2) \\\\  & =-5(\\frac{3}{2}-1)(\\frac{3}{2}-2) \\\\  & =-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{5}{4}),$ and the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\frac{5}{4}].$\n\n![](images/42/426a8277921ca2c8282567eeb076c3dcf1f0f1c729c4ebd2e5d624f51b78d61e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561069 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186561071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561069 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "294ef667-0d61-5f95-93c6-77309e10d176" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561069 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186560980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561071 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186561083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561071 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "459a4996-3ca0-5e5e-9a1f-8d2cd29c20c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561071 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186561015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561083 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "97fce570-7fc4-5f25-8fc4-16001b69205d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561083 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186561042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561596 #edb/ref 1080 "[-2,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561596 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561596 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0541d29e-1a3d-5725-a3e8-30e78b5ddec7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561599 #edb/ref 1080 "x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 1